# GitHub backlog project

Grid Dungeon required-feature work is tracked on **[Codename: GridDungeon](https://github.com/users/miramocha/projects/3)** (GitHub Project #3, owner `miramocha`).

## Config file (read first)

Before searching for a project URL or asking the user which board to use:

1. Read **`.cursor/backlog-project.json`** at the repo root of any open workspace folder (`griddungeon-game` or `griddungeon-design-docs`).
2. Use `owner` + `number` (or `projectUrl`) for `gh project view`, `gh project item-list`, and `gh project item-edit`.
3. Honor `readyStatus`, `backlogStatus`, `priorityOrder`, `excludeLabels`, `preferLabels`, and `limit` from the config.
4. When both repos are open, prefer issues whose repository matches `repoPrefer` (`game` vs `docs`) when ranking ties.

The only per-repo difference is **`repoPrefer`** — project identity and column names are the same in both copies.

## Pull order

Wave labels (`pull-w01` … `pull-w08`) are legacy labels; new work uses `required` / `optional` labels. Scope authority: [docs/00-release-scope.md](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-design-docs/blob/main/docs/00-release-scope.md) (`pullOrderDoc` in JSON). Historical wave table: git history of [docs/00-release-scope.md](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-design-docs/blob/main/docs/00-release-scope.md).

## Skill workflow

For “next ticket”, “pull backlog”, or “what should I work on” requests, follow the **pull-next-backlog-ticket** skill after reading this config.

## Do not

- Ask the user for the project URL when `.cursor/backlog-project.json` exists in an open workspace root.
- Invent work that is not on the project board.
